<newsitem itemid="76902" id="root" date="1996-09-25" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Alexon first-half profits rise.</title>
<headline>Alexon first-half profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>26 weeks to July 27</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		4.16 profit	  vs 0.86 loss</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 nil		    vs same</p>
<p> Pretax		     3.03		   vs 0.14</p>
<p> Turnover		   57.20		  vs 47.76</p>
<p> Operating result	 3.19		   vs 0.64</p>
<p> Interest		   0.16 debit	   vs 0.49</p>
<p> Tax			  nil		    vs same</p>
<p>NOTE - Alexon Group Plc makes and retails clothing. It said trading in the first eight weeks of the second half had seen like-for-like sales increase by 15 percent with all brands performing well. The group plans to resume paying dividends on both classes of preference shares and accumulated arrears in March and April 1997 if trading is satisfactory.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
